<CaseStudyPage title="Case study: Vay" description="Creating a customer-facing mobile app for remote controlled cars in Las Vegas.">
  <h3>Mobile app</h3>
  <p>Vay is redefining urban mobility with remotely driven vehicles. We joined at the beginning of the company's journey to transform its proof-of-concept customer app into a fully fledged mobile application, and have supported the project with our mobile expertise since then.</p>
  <p>The app lets customers find and book a vehicle, unlock it on delivery, inspect service areas, end rides, and complete payments. Today it has a consistent 4.8-star rating in both Google Play and the App Store.</p>
  <h3>Challenges</h3>
  <p>The work required close collaboration among teams across Europe and Las Vegas, plus integration with a hardware device in each vehicle using Bluetooth.</p>
  <h3>Process</h3>
  <p>Clear asynchronous communication, architecture decision records, and cross-system debugging helped the teams make complex features dependable. We also built direct Bluetooth Low Energy communication so customers could unlock a vehicle even with poor mobile connectivity.</p>
  <h3>Conclusion</h3>
  <p>Helping move the product from a rough prototype to a functional, innovative service has been valuable both technically and organisationally.</p>
</CaseStudyPage>
